PART 7 — EXPORT AND IMPORT SECURITY

Inspect the current workflow JSON export/import system.

The export format must never contain:

- Plaintext passwords.
- Decrypted credential payloads.
- Encryption keys.
- Authentication tokens.
- Temporary secret values.

Exports may contain opaque credential reference IDs only if doing so is safe and useful.

Imported workflows must not be trusted automatically.

Validate:

- Workflow structure.
- Credential references.
- Locator data.
- Origin bindings.
- Action types.
- Unsupported or malformed fields.

If an imported workflow references a credential that does not exist locally, mark that credential step as unassigned.

Never attempt to recover credentials from an imported workflow.

Do not overwrite existing credentials automatically during import.

