PART 8 — PRIVACY AND MEMORY HYGIENE

Implement practical protections against accidental secret retention.

Requirements:

- Never log credential values.
- Never include credentials in exception messages.
- Never include credentials in execution history.
- Never include credentials in analytics.
- Never include credentials in crash reports.
- Never include credentials in workflow exports.
- Never include credentials in screenshots or debugging overlays.
- Never place passwords in clipboard automatically.
- Never persist plaintext passwords in DataStore or SharedPreferences.
- Avoid writing decrypted credentials to temporary files.
- Avoid unnecessary copies of secret strings.
- Clear mutable buffers and references when possible.
- Do not claim that garbage collection securely erases immutable strings.

Explain any unavoidable transient exposure in the implementation report.

Do not make unrealistic claims that Android or Kotlin can guarantee perfect erasure of all in-memory secret copies.

